course: dictionary
lesson: 6359
title: Reading mph on signs and in sums
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: mph is short for miles per hour. It tells you how many miles something travels in one hour, so it is a unit of speed. When you see a number before mph, read it as "that many miles every hour".
explain: The words around mph are its context. «A car at 30 mph needs about 23 m to stop» tells you that 30 mph is a speed, and that a faster car needs a longer distance to stop. The number 23 is in metres, so the sentence is about distance too.
explain: In maths, speed is worked out with a simple rule: speed = distance ÷ time. If a cyclist goes 20 miles in 1 hour, the speed is 20 mph. Always check the units: miles and hours give mph, and metres and seconds would give a different unit.
fact: mph is short for miles per hour.
fact: mph is a unit of speed, used on road signs and in cars in the UK and the USA.
fact: «A 30 mph zone» is a road where the speed limit is 30 miles per hour.
fact: «An electric bike motor must stop helping at about 15.5 mph (25 km/h).»
fact: Speed cameras measure speed with radar or by timing a car between two points, and there are 20 mph zones near schools because a person hit at 20 mph is much less likely to be killed than at 30 mph.
exercise: What does mph stand for? | miles per house | *miles per hour | metres per hour | minutes per hour
exercise: «A car at 30 mph needs about 23 m to stop.» What is mph measuring here? | distance | weight | *speed | time
exercise: A car travels 60 miles in 1 hour. Using speed = distance ÷ time, what is its speed? | 61 mph | 1 mph | 59 mph | *60 mph
test: Why are there 20 mph zones near schools? | *Because a person hit at 20 mph is much less likely to be killed than at 30 mph | To stop people walking on the pavement | To make roads wider | To make cars go faster
test: «In the UK the motor must stop helping at about 15.5 mph (25 km/h).» What does 15.5 mph mean? | 15.5 minutes | 15 miles per second | 15.5 hours | *15.5 miles every hour, about 25 km/h
exam: A car travels at 40 mph for one hour. How far does it go? | 400 miles | 0.4 miles | *40 miles | 4 miles
